//
// Live smoke test: end-to-end BTC transfer from a QuipWallet on testnet.
//
// PERSISTENT STATE: every WOTS+ private key, vault id, and Arch/Bitcoin txid
// generated by this script is written to a state file (default
// `keys/smoke-wallet-<vaultId>.json`, or `--state-file <path>`). If the run
// times out or crashes mid-flow, re-run with `--resume <state-file>` to pick
// up exactly where it left off — no fresh wallets minted, no UTXOs stranded.
//
// Flow (each step is idempotent and skipped if already done in state):
//   1. Verify the deployer/owner Arch account is anchored (anchor it if not).
//   2. Generate two WOTS+ keypairs (current pq_owner + rotation target pq_next)
//      and persist them to disk.
//   3. Build & broadcast TX-A (4 outputs: wallet anchor, wallet non-anchor,
//      deployer fee-input, deployer change). Persist its txid.
//   4. Submit createWallet (anchor=TX-A:0); wait for readback.
//   5. Build the fee tx (single input from TX-A:2, NONE|ANYONECANPAY-signed,
//      not broadcast).
//   6. Build BtcTransferMessage, sign with WOTS+, submit btcTransfer Arch tx
//      with explicit ComputeBudget prefix. Persist Arch txid.
//   7. Poll for processed status -> recover Bitcoin txid the runtime broadcast.
//   8. Wait for that Bitcoin tx in mempool; verify a 1500-sat UTXO landed back
//      at the deployer P2TR (round-trip).
//
// Run (fresh): npx tsx scripts/smoke-btc-transfer.ts
// Run (resume): npx tsx scripts/smoke-btc-transfer.ts --resume <state-file>

